# Allow-list for scripts/fitness/no-cross-module-imports.py
#
# Format (one rule per line, '#' starts a comment):
#     <path-glob>: <module-glob>
#   path-glob   fnmatch pattern vs the file path relative to its addon root
#               (posix separators; '*' also matches '/').
#   module-glob fnmatch pattern vs the imported dotted module; a rule also
#               covers submodules (odoo.addons.sale.tests.common.x).
# A rule without ':' is a module-glob that applies to every path.
# Runtime-computed imports (importlib/__import__ with a non-literal name)
# match the module name '<dynamic>'.
#
# EVERY rule needs a justification: a non-empty comment inline
# ('<rule>  # why') or on the line directly above (no blank line between).
# A rule without one is a usage error (exit 2). Allow-listed imports are
# still reported as ALLOWED lines; they never pass silently.
#
# Tests may reuse another addon's test fixtures (standard Odoo practice).
tests/**: odoo.addons.*.tests.common
